Well that was fun.

I had acquired a lot of junk, and had altar-BUCed it, so I decided to 
read some of the scrolls.

So I took my clothes (I was a monk) in case one was destroy armour.  The 
first one I read was ... create monster, of course!  Lots of monsters.

Okay, okay, don't panic, I'm surrounded, what's the most important 
thing?  Ah, yes pick up armour.  So I pick it up, then the first attack: 
"The dust vortex engulfs you!"  Well, could be worse I suppose.  The I 
think: wait a moment, maybe...

"You put on an uncursed rotted +1 robe."
...
"You put on an uncursed +0 pair of iron shoes."
...
"You put on an uncursed +2 pair of leather gloves."
...
"You put on an uncursed +0 orcish helm."

Handy, eh?

So, I have managed to get dressed in the middle of a crowd of monsters 
and have lost only a few HP.  Neat, eh?  (Well, dumb luck actually, but 
never mind.  Of course I didn't survive.  None of my kit was useful in 
the situation, even if I had been able to read the scrolls, though I had 
time to try most of it out inside the dust vortex.)

Has anyone else here managed to pull off a trick as silly or amazing as 
this one?

